      "pot": {
        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define variables\n    market_index = [3, 2, 4, 5, 6]\n    nav_change = [5, 4, 6, 7, 9]\n\n    # Calculate the slope using the least squares formula\n    n = len(market_index)\n    sum_x = sum(market_index)\n    sum_y = sum(nav_change)\n    sum_xy = sum(x * y for x, y in zip(market_index, nav_change))\n    sum_x_squared = sum(x ** 2 for x in market_index)\n\n    slope = (\n        n * sum_xy - sum_x * sum_y\n    ) / (\n        n * sum_x_squared - sum_x ** 2\n    )\n\n    # Return the slope rounded to two decimal places\n    return round(slope, 2)\n```",
